# PhiCad Altium profile — PROVISIONAL hotkey overlay.
#
# Format is KiCad's own: <action.name>\t<Key>\t<AltKey>, parsed by
# ReadHotKeyConfig (common/hotkeys_basic.cpp).  Lines starting with # are
# stripped by phicad-profile and never reach the installed file: KiCad would
# store a comment as an action named "#..." and keep rewriting it forever.
#
# GROUNDING CAVEAT.  phicad/research/altium/ux.md was produced with no live
# Altium Designer to check against (its report contract records BLOCKED), so
# these are the mappings that are both widely documented for AD and provable
# here, not a transcription of a real install.  Spot-check them against the
# Altium version you actually use before trusting the file.
#
# Every line keeps KiCad's own default as the ALT key, so nothing a KiCad user
# already knows stops working -- and if macOS swallows the Cmd combination the
# original key is still there.
#
# Constraints these mappings were checked against:
#   * Ctrl+ and Cmd+ both parse to MD_CTRL on every platform, but Alt+ parses
#     only off macOS (MODIFIER_ALT is Option+ here), so no Alt binding is used.
#   * an unparseable key name does not fall back -- it silently REMOVES the
#     action's default binding, so every literal below is from hotkeyNameList.
#   * no combination below collides with another action registered in the same
#     editor (checked against every .DefaultHotkey in the tree).
#
# Deliberately NOT mapped, and why:
#   Ctrl+M  (AD Measure Distance) collides with pcbnew.InteractiveMove.
#           moveIndividually, and Cmd+M is the macOS minimise gesture.
#   L       (AD View Configurations) collides with pcbnew.EditorControl.toggleLock.
#   Q       (AD toggle units) collides with eeschema.InteractiveDrawing.placeNoConnect.
#   2 / 3   (AD 2D/3D view) collide with the length-tuner adjustments, and KiCad
#           has no 2D-view action to bind the other half to.
#   F11     (AD Properties panel) is the macOS Show Desktop key; the Properties
#           and Appearance panels already have left-toolbar toggles instead.

# AD Ctrl+W = Interactively Route Connections; KiCad ships X.
pcbnew.InteractiveRouter.SingleTrack	Ctrl+W	X
# AD Ctrl+W = Place Wire; KiCad ships W.
eeschema.InteractiveDrawingLineWireBus.drawWires	Ctrl+W	W
# AD Ctrl+H = Select > Connected Copper; KiCad ships U.
pcbnew.InteractiveSelection.SelectConnection	Ctrl+H	U
# AD Ctrl+PgDn = Fit Document; KiCad ships Ctrl+0.
common.Control.zoomFitScreen	Ctrl+PgDn	Ctrl+0
